# Security probes

- Map the untrusted edge (form fields, query, headers, uploads) before probing.
- Pair every probe with a **mutant fixture** that embeds the fault class under
  test; CI/local runs must kill that mutant or the probe is not ready.
- Prefer observable effects: script execution, reflected raw HTML, SQL/error
  oracle, privilege change, unexpected redirect — not generic 500s alone.
- Keep payloads and oracles in code next to the bot; do not rely on manual
  scanner dumps as findings.
- AuthN/AuthZ checks: identity from credential, never from a client-supplied id.
